WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:06.020
Hello, and welcome to your second drink of Job Fair.
你好，欢迎收听《求职展销会》的第二杯特饮。

2
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:12.660
We had a lot to say in this episode about washing our hands, blisters, and golf courses.
我们在这一期里有很多话要说，关于洗手、水泡和高尔夫球场。

3
00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:14.620
Such a weird liSt.
真是个奇怪的清单。

4
00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:20.560
We also got tons of mail about the deleted cold open that I had shared about for this episode.
我们还收到了大量关于我分享的那段本集被删冷开场的邮件。

5
00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:23.100
It's where Michael loses all of the stuff in the toilet.
就是迈克尔把所有东西都掉进马桶里的那一幕。

6
00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:23.760
Yep.
没错。

7
00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:26.900
It was in deleted scenes, and I wasn't able to play it,
它原本在删减片段里，我没能播出来，

8
00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:29.740
but it's been added back to the Peacock Superfan version.
但它已经被加回了 Peacock 超级粉丝版本中。

9
00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:34.460
It starts with Michael screaming from the bathroom, and Dwight rushes off to help him,
故事始于迈克尔在卫生间的尖叫，德怀特冲过去帮忙，

10
00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:39.260
and then they both walk into the bullpen, and Dwight is carrying a bunch of stuff in a paper towel.
然后他们一起走进开放式办公区，德怀特用纸巾包着一堆东西。

11
00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:40.060
Let's hear it.
让我们听听看。

12
00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:42.590
No!
不！

13
00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:45.930
No, no, no, no, no, no!
不，不，不，不，不，不！

14
00:00:56.230 --> 00:00:59.210
I do not want to talk about it.
我不想谈这个。

15
00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:00.090
Unbelievable.
难以置信。

16
00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:02.390
That—okay.
那——好吧。

17
00:01:02.570 --> 00:01:03.430
What happened, Michael?
怎么了，迈克尔？

18
00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:08.030
Oh, wouldn't you like to know what happened in the bathroom by myself, pervy?
哦，你是不是很想知道我自己一个人在卫生间里发生了什么，你这个老色鬼？

19
00:01:08.990 --> 00:01:13.870
I—suffice to say, I had finished my business, I was just checking to make sure everything was fine,
我——总而言之，我办完了事，我只是在检查一切是否正常，

20
00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:20.170
and my cell phone fell out and on, not in, but, like, on the rim, and then—
然后我的手机掉了出来，掉在——不是掉进，而是像掉在边缘上，接着——

21
00:01:20.170 --> 00:01:20.670
It fell in.
掉进去了。

22
00:01:21.070 --> 00:01:22.510
Just let me tell the story, okay?
让我把话说完，好吗？

23
00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:25.690
Jim, I knocked it with my knee, and then it fell in.
吉姆，我用膝盖碰了一下，然后它就掉进去了。

24
00:01:25.790 --> 00:01:29.570
And then I leaned over and looked, and my Bluetooth fell out of my ear, and that fell in.
接着我探身去看，我的蓝牙耳机从耳朵里掉了出来，那个也掉进去了。

25
00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:29.790
Bluetooth.
蓝牙耳机。

26
00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:32.570
And then I got flustered, and everything started falling in.
然后我慌了，所有东西开始往下掉。

27
00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:39.390
My wallet fell in, my tip calculator, my candy corn, my white strips, all fell in to the toilet.
我的钱包掉进去了，我的小费计算器掉进去了，我的玉米糖掉进去了，我的牙齿美白贴条，全都掉进了马桶里。

28
00:01:39.630 --> 00:01:40.710
And your keys fell in?
连你的钥匙也掉进去了？

29
00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:42.810
I threw the keys in out of anger.
钥匙是我气愤之下扔进去的。

30
00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:43.230
Right.
好吧。

31
00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:45.550
This cannot happen again!
这种事不能再发生了！

32
00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:46.750
That's what you said last time.
你上次也是这么说的。

33
00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:47.710
I know I did!
我知道我是这么说的！

34
00:01:48.790 --> 00:01:49.930
Phyllis, this is not funny.
菲莉丝，这不好笑。

35
00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:51.010
This is not funny.
这一点也不好笑。

36
00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:53.590
Well, technically it is.
嗯，严格来说确实挺好笑的。

37
00:01:53.710 --> 00:01:55.550
Toilet humor, which you claim to enjoy.
厕所笑话，而你声称自己很喜欢。

38
00:01:55.770 --> 00:01:57.910
It is not toilet humor, it is toilet tragedy.
这不是厕所笑话，这是厕所悲剧。

39
00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:07.230
Hey!
嘿！

40
00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:08.930
Hey!
嘿！

41
00:02:09.130 --> 00:02:09.710
You know what?
你知道吗？

42
00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:14.230
This is the best thing that ever happened to me.
这是发生在我身上最好的事。

43
00:02:15.070 --> 00:02:18.410
This whole scene, please, you guys, it's so worth a watch.
整场戏，求求你们，真的非常值得一看。

44
00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:19.470
It's so funny.
太搞笑了。

45
00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:21.810
I can't believe that this was cut.
我真不敢相信这段被剪掉了。

46
00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:24.750
I would have cut anything out of the episode.
为了保留它，我宁愿剪掉这集的任何其他内容。

47
00:02:24.850 --> 00:02:30.270
I mean, it's a great episode, but, like, I feel like more should have been done to keep this cold open.
我的意思是，这是一集很棒的节目，但我觉得应该做更多努力来保留这个冷开场。

48
00:02:30.470 --> 00:02:34.070
I say it in our breakdown, but I remember from the table read,
我在我们的解析里也说过，我记得在围读剧本时，

49
00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:37.870
laughing so hard when he says he threw his keys in out of anger.
听到他说他是气愤之下把钥匙扔进去时，大家笑得前仰后合。

50
00:02:38.110 --> 00:02:38.570
I know.
我知道。

51
00:02:38.770 --> 00:02:41.010
Also, how much shit does he keep in his pocket?
还有，他口袋里到底塞了多少破烂？

52
00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:42.090
So much.
塞得老多了。

53
00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:44.110
How did the tip calculator get involved?
小费计算器是怎么扯进来的？

54
00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:44.410
I know.
我懂。

55
00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:44.950
I don't know.
我不知道。

56
00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:45.490
I don't know.
我不知道。

57
00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:50.550
So after this, there is a scene where Michael comes out of his office,
所以接下来，有一场戏是迈克尔从办公室走出来，

58
00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:52.590
and he is holding a new invention.
手里拿着一项新发明。

59
00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:57.890
This is the invention that is going to save you from having your stuff fall in the toilet.
这就是那个能拯救你的东西，免得你的随身物品掉进马桶里。

60
00:02:58.190 --> 00:02:58.410
Right.
没错。

61
00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:02.490
And you described it from the script when we first broke down the episode,
我们在刚开始梳理这集剧本时，你根据剧本描述过它，

62
00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:06.230
but, oh, my gosh, seeing the footage again,
但是，天哪，再次看到这段素材，

63
00:03:07.490 --> 00:03:09.530
Michael is showing it off.
迈克尔正在炫耀它。

64
00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:10.670
He's standing at reception.
他站在前台那里。

65
00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:14.590
So I'm in this two-shot with him, and he's holding up his invention.
我和他拍了这个双人镜头，他正举着他的发明。

66
00:03:14.770 --> 00:03:19.590
And I just remember the first time I saw it, I immediately started laughing.
我只记得我第一次看到它的时候，直接就笑喷了。

67
00:03:19.730 --> 00:03:22.190
This is something that Phil Shea had to make,
这是菲尔·谢伊必须做出来的一个道具，

68
00:03:23.210 --> 00:03:26.870
and I had not seen it yet, and it broke me.
我当时还没见过，它让我彻底破功了。

69
00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:28.430
Well, it's just so ridiculous.
对啊，这太荒谬了。

70
00:03:28.630 --> 00:03:32.930
It's like the head of a tennis racket, but then the handle's been chopped off,
它就像是一个网球拍的拍头，但把手给砍掉了，

71
00:03:33.010 --> 00:03:38.370
but then it's like a dishwashing brush attached, but then it has a chain.
然后上面还连着一个洗碗刷，接着它还有一条链子。

72
00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:39.230
Yeah.
对。

73
00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:41.670
You know the thing you wash your dishes with, the brush?
你知道你用来洗碗的那个东西吗，就是刷子？

74
00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:41.970
Yeah.
对。

75
00:03:41.970 --> 00:03:46.610
Like, imagine that dangling from the top of a tennis racket by a chain.
就像，想象一下那个东西用一条链子挂在网球拍的顶端。

76
00:03:46.770 --> 00:03:47.410
So I guess the—
所以我想—

77
00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:49.330
So you put the racket over the toilet bowl.
所以你要把网球拍放在马桶盆上方。

78
00:03:49.510 --> 00:03:49.890
Right.
没错。

79
00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:53.790
And you have to do your business through the racket threads.
然后你必须透过网球拍的线网去解决你的内急。

80
00:03:53.990 --> 00:03:58.430
Yes, and then you use the brush because, as Michael says, it's self-cleaning.
对，然后你得用那个刷子，因为正如迈克尔所说，它是自动清洗的。

81
00:03:58.530 --> 00:03:58.710
Yes.
对。

82
00:03:58.830 --> 00:04:00.910
Which, I mean, it's you cleaning.
也就是，其实是你自己在清洗。

83
00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:01.650
It's you cleaning.
是你自己在清洗。

84
00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:02.410
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

85
00:04:02.590 --> 00:04:03.030
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

86
00:04:03.190 --> 00:04:06.130
But you clearly can only go number one.
但你显然只能上小号。

87
00:04:07.790 --> 00:04:13.050
I mean, I would think, but it's just—it's so absurd,
我是觉得吧，但这简直—太荒谬了，

88
00:04:13.050 --> 00:04:15.450
but it's also just one of the funniest things.
但这也是最好笑的事情之一。

89
00:04:15.890 --> 00:04:17.530
I'm so glad it's in the supervan.
我太高兴它能被收录在加长版里了。

90
00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:17.930
Same.
我也是。

91
00:04:17.930 --> 00:04:21.130
Okay, well, we also got this letter from Sandra P.
好的，我们还收到了桑德拉·P发来的这封信。

92
00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:22.310
Sandra says,
桑德拉说，

93
00:04:22.450 --> 00:04:26.990
Whenever I watch Job Fair, I find it interesting that the series starts with downsizing
每当我观看《招聘会》时，我都觉得很有趣，剧集一开始讲的是裁员、

94
00:04:26.990 --> 00:04:29.590
and closing branches and firing people,
关闭分公司和解雇员工，

95
00:04:29.650 --> 00:04:33.750
and now they are actively recruiting people at a job fair.
而现在他们却在招聘会上积极招募人员。

96
00:04:34.270 --> 00:04:36.050
Michael should have hired Devin back.
迈克尔本该把德文重新雇回来的。

97
00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:40.090
I love this letter because I didn't even put that together.
我很喜欢这封信，因为我之前根本没把这两件事联系起来。

98
00:04:40.450 --> 00:04:46.490
Yes, the whole series of The Office of season like one through three is just about downsizing.
没错，《办公室》从第一季到第三季的整个系列都在讲裁员的事。

99
00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:47.610
Are we going to lose our job?
我们会失业吗？

100
00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:49.070
Stanford closes.
斯坦福分公司关闭了。

101
00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:49.610
Yes.
对。

102
00:04:49.770 --> 00:04:56.150
We're constantly worried about losing our jobs, but now we're at a job fair.
我们总是担心失去工作，但现在我们在招聘会上。

103
00:04:56.150 --> 00:05:00.150
Yeah, now we're recruiting people to work for us that we can't afford to hire.
对，现在我们在招募我们根本请不起的员工。

104
00:05:00.510 --> 00:05:01.290
So true.
确实如此。

105
00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:06.890
So, you know, in this episode when Pam has to go find a second sheet of paper,
所以，你知道，这一集里帕姆不得不去找第二张纸的时候，

106
00:05:07.170 --> 00:05:08.550
do you remember that whole thing?
你还记得整段剧情吗？

107
00:05:08.710 --> 00:05:12.010
Like, Michael is like, bring one piece of paper.
迈克尔当时说，只带一张纸就行。

108
00:05:12.170 --> 00:05:12.350
Yeah.
对。

109
00:05:12.350 --> 00:05:17.710
And then somebody signs their name on it, so she has to go find another piece of paper.
然后有人在上面签了字，所以她不得不去找另一张纸。

110
00:05:18.370 --> 00:05:24.030
Well, she goes to her old art room, and along the way, she sees a photo of Roy in the trophy
她去了她以前的美术教室，在路上，她在走廊的奖杯陈列柜里

111
00:05:24.030 --> 00:05:24.930
case in the hallway.
看到了罗伊的照片。

112
00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:30.030
He's in, like, his football gear, and it says he was all-city team, first place, 1995.
他穿着橄榄球装备，上面写着他是全城第一阵容，1995年。

113
00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:33.430
Pam stops, and she looks at it, and she says,
帕姆停下脚步，看着它说，

114
00:05:33.530 --> 00:05:35.810
Roy, nine years of my life.
罗伊，我生命中的九年。

115
00:05:36.450 --> 00:05:39.390
Then she goes into the art room, and she's kind of looking to see,
然后她走进美术教室，四处张望，

116
00:05:39.590 --> 00:05:42.050
oh, my gosh, I wonder if it's still up.
天哪，我想知道它还在不在。

117
00:05:42.350 --> 00:05:42.910
On display.
还在展出。

118
00:05:43.290 --> 00:05:43.870
Yeah, Pam's art.
对，帕姆的美术作品。

119
00:05:43.990 --> 00:05:47.250
Some art piece that she was obviously proud of, and it's not.
那是她显然很自豪的一件艺术品，但已经不在了。

120
00:05:47.690 --> 00:05:50.670
Well, I love this observation we got from Patrick R.
我很喜欢爱达荷州博伊西的帕特里克·R.

121
00:05:50.790 --> 00:05:53.110
in Boise, Idaho, who said,
发给我们的这个观察，他说，

122
00:05:53.270 --> 00:05:57.870
I always thought it was an extra dig at Pam that Roy's photo was still displayed,
我一直觉得罗伊的照片还在展出，而帕姆的艺术品却没了，这是对帕姆的又一次挖苦。

123
00:05:57.870 --> 00:05:59.210
but her art was gone.
他们留下了他的成就，却没有留下她的。

124
00:05:59.430 --> 00:06:02.150
They left up his accomplishment, but not hers.
这太奇怪了。

125
00:06:02.450 --> 00:06:03.150
It's so weird.
我从来没把这些联系在一起。

126
00:06:03.150 --> 00:06:04.250
I never put that together.
我从没想过这就像是一种额外的挖苦。

127
00:06:05.430 --> 00:06:09.650
I never put together that, like, it was, like, this added dig.
对。

128
00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:10.390
Yeah.
我喜欢这个细节。

129
00:06:10.390 --> 00:06:11.270
And I liked that.
我确信这是编剧刻意安排的。

130
00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:13.310
I'm sure that was intentional by the writers.
我第一次看的时候漏掉了。

131
00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:14.710
I missed it the first time.
这也算是一种，我不知道你们成长过程中有没有在学校经历过，

132
00:06:14.910 --> 00:06:20.390
It's also sort of that, and I don't know if you guys had experienced this in any of your schools
但我确实记得我们橄榄球队的预算最多，而美术和戏剧社

133
00:06:20.390 --> 00:06:26.750
growing up, but I do remember our football team had the biggest budget, and our arts and theater
却没有。

134
00:06:26.750 --> 00:06:27.350
did not.
当然。

135
00:06:27.510 --> 00:06:27.830
Sure.
所以有点这种感觉，当然，那些奖杯肯定还在。

136
00:06:27.830 --> 00:06:32.230
So, a little bit that, of course, of course, those trophies are still around.
对。

137
00:06:32.610 --> 00:06:32.930
Yes.
而且，你根本拿不到奖杯。

138
00:06:33.110 --> 00:06:35.930
And also, like, you don't get trophies.
学校里根本没有给艺术生的奖杯陈列柜。

139
00:06:36.070 --> 00:06:40.190
There's no trophy case for the artists in the school.
辩论队的也没有。

140
00:06:40.770 --> 00:06:41.850
The debaters.
嗯哼。

141
00:06:42.370 --> 00:06:42.610
Mm-hmm.
也许运动员有。

142
00:06:42.610 --> 00:06:43.910
Maybe the athletes.
最佳独幕剧。

143
00:06:44.350 --> 00:06:45.370
Best one-act play.
也许某处有个牌匾。

144
00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:47.090
Maybe there's a plaque somewhere.
对。

145
00:06:47.470 --> 00:06:47.810
Yeah.
在后台休息室里。

146
00:06:47.890 --> 00:06:48.750
Back in the green room.
或者是演讲比赛的。

147
00:06:48.870 --> 00:06:49.670
Or speech.
对。

148
00:06:49.970 --> 00:06:50.310
Yeah.
最后，我们收到了詹妮弗·M.的信，她说，

149
00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:55.870
Well, finally, we got this letter from Jennifer M., who said,
你们在播客里没有聊到查理·麦克德莫特扮演那个酷炫的高中男生。

150
00:06:56.230 --> 00:07:00.410
you didn't talk about Charlie McDermott playing the cool high school guy on the podcaSt.
查理·麦克德莫特扮演那个酷炫的高中男生。

151
00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:04.090
Did he act in the job fair while he was on The Middle?
他在出演《左右不逢源》期间演过求职会这一集吗？

152
00:07:05.410 --> 00:07:11.190
Well, first off, my apologies for not giving Charlie McDermott a proper guest star breakdown.
嗯，首先，我为之前没有对查理·麦克德莫特作出一份合适的客串演员介绍而道歉。

153
00:07:11.550 --> 00:07:12.570
I'm going to do it now.
