I Googled, there is a country club of Scranton that offers golf, as well as a few other golf
我用谷歌查了，斯克兰顿乡村俱乐部可以打高尔夫，斯克兰顿地区附近还有其他几家高尔夫

317
00:13:33.600 --> 00:13:35.020
courses near the Scranton area.
球场。

318
00:13:35.020 --> 00:13:37.720
I don't know which course this is supposed to be.
我不知道这应该是哪个球场。

319
00:13:37.720 --> 00:13:42.560
But we filmed at Vista Valencia golf course in Santa Clarita.
但我们是在圣克拉利塔的维斯塔瓦伦西亚高尔夫球场拍的。

320
00:13:43.440 --> 00:13:45.740
It's a 27-hole facility.
这是一个拥有27个洞的设施。

321
00:13:45.740 --> 00:13:51.760
It has an 18-hole par 61 course and a 9-hole par 3 course.
它有一个18洞标准杆61杆的球场和一个9洞标准杆3杆的球场。

322
00:13:51.980 --> 00:13:53.780
Now, here's what I found very interesting.
现在，我觉得非常有意思的是这个。

323
00:13:53.980 --> 00:13:55.100
Maybe only to me.
也许只有我觉得有意思。

324
00:13:55.480 --> 00:13:56.320
Let's hear it.
说来听听。

325
00:13:56.320 --> 00:14:01.380
The prices to play depend on what day you're playing and also what time you arrive.
打球的价格取决于你哪天去打，还取决于你到达的时间。

326
00:14:01.700 --> 00:14:05.640
It's least expensive to go during the week in the afternoon.
工作日下午去是最便宜的。

327
00:14:05.940 --> 00:14:10.600
If you come first thing in the morning, it's going to cost you $24.50 to walk the course
如果你一大早来，步行打全场需要花24.50美元

328
00:14:10.600 --> 00:14:12.460
or $36.50 to ride it.
坐球车则需要36.50美元。

329
00:14:12.580 --> 00:14:18.060
If you come at 3 o'clock, it's only $13 to walk it and $23.50 to ride it.
如果你下午3点来，步行只要13美元，坐球车只要23.50美元。

330
00:14:18.200 --> 00:14:21.220
But why is it more expensive to ride it?
但为什么坐球车反而更贵呢？

331
00:14:21.300 --> 00:14:22.740
Is it because it comes with the cart?
是因为包含了球车本身的费用吗？

332
00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:24.240
I couldn't find that information.
我没能查到这方面的信息。

333
00:14:24.240 --> 00:14:29.340
It seems like you'd flow faster if you're riding it than if you're walking it.
感觉坐球车应该比步行移动得更快才对。

334
00:14:29.600 --> 00:14:30.360
Guess what, everybody?
大家猜怎么着？

335
00:14:30.520 --> 00:14:31.780
I don't know a lot about golfing.
我对高尔夫并不太了解。

336
00:14:33.020 --> 00:14:35.480
This is why I'm quiet because I'm like, I don't know.
这就是为什么我很安静，因为我在想，我不知道。

337
00:14:35.780 --> 00:14:37.400
But here's the big kicker.
但最厉害的来了。

338
00:14:37.500 --> 00:14:40.000
And this is why I think you and I need to go to this golf course.
这也是为什么我觉得你和我需要去一趟这个高尔夫球场。

339
00:14:40.240 --> 00:14:40.520
Okay.
好吧。

340
00:14:40.920 --> 00:14:42.920
They have something called foot golf.
他们有一种叫足式高尔夫的东西。

341
00:14:43.240 --> 00:14:44.080
Foot golf?
足式高尔夫？

342
00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:45.680
I'd never heard of it.
我以前从没听说过。

343
00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:46.860
It's a real thing.
这是真的存在的。

344
00:14:47.020 --> 00:14:49.660
It's a combination of soccer and golf.
它是足球和高尔夫的结合。

345
00:14:49.980 --> 00:14:50.900
And hacky sack.
还有沙包球。

346
00:14:51.360 --> 00:14:53.460
I think you could hacky and sack it in there.
我觉得你可以在里面玩沙包球。

347
00:14:53.460 --> 00:14:58.800
There's basically a special golf course, but the holes are really big and you kick the
基本上就是有一个特殊的高尔夫球场，但是洞非常大，你要把

348
00:14:58.800 --> 00:15:00.800
ball down the course into the hole.
球沿着球场踢进洞里。

349
00:15:01.200 --> 00:15:01.540
Okay.
好吧。

350
00:15:02.020 --> 00:15:02.480
Foot golf.
足式高尔夫。

351
00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:05.360
Maybe we could frolf and then foot golf.
也许我们可以先玩飞盘高尔夫，再去踢足高尔夫。

352
00:15:05.780 --> 00:15:10.620
I would foot golf if there was like a pony keg set up on like the eighth hole.
如果第八洞那里能架个小啤酒桶的话，我倒是挺愿意踢足高尔夫的。

353
00:15:10.760 --> 00:15:14.700
So like you kick your ball, then you have a beer, then you kick your ball.
就是你踢一脚球，然后喝一杯啤酒，再踢一脚球。

354
00:15:14.820 --> 00:15:16.020
What's a pony keg?
什么叫小啤酒桶？

355
00:15:16.120 --> 00:15:16.880
A pony keg?
小啤酒桶？

356
00:15:17.020 --> 00:15:17.280
Isn't that?
不是吗？

357
00:15:17.400 --> 00:15:18.620
Don't y'all have pony kegs?
难道你们那儿没有小啤酒桶吗？

358
00:15:18.760 --> 00:15:19.500
It's like a party keg.
就像派对用的小桶一样。

359
00:15:19.620 --> 00:15:21.140
It's like a mini keg of beer.
就像一小桶啤酒。

360
00:15:21.140 --> 00:15:22.000
A pony keg?
小啤酒桶？

361
00:15:22.120 --> 00:15:22.320
Anyone?
有人知道吗？

362
00:15:22.940 --> 00:15:23.380
Sam?
萨姆？

363
00:15:23.660 --> 00:15:24.100
Cassie?
凯茜？

364
00:15:24.240 --> 00:15:24.720
Pony keg?
小啤酒桶？

365
00:15:24.800 --> 00:15:25.320
Ever heard of it?
没听说过吗？

366
00:15:26.120 --> 00:15:28.040
A pony keg is a mini keg?
小啤酒桶就是迷你啤酒桶？

367
00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:28.680
Yeah.
对啊。

368
00:15:28.860 --> 00:15:29.840
It's like a baby keg.
就像一个婴儿桶一样。

369
00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:30.400
No, you're right.
不对，你说得对。

370
00:15:30.460 --> 00:15:31.860
Pony keg is a quarter keg.
小啤酒桶其实是四分之一桶。

371
00:15:31.920 --> 00:15:32.160
Yeah!
对啊！

372
00:15:32.400 --> 00:15:33.060
Thank you!
谢谢你！

373
00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:35.160
What's a half keg called?
那半桶叫什么？

374
00:15:37.390 --> 00:15:37.830
Silence.
一片寂静。

375
00:15:41.920 --> 00:15:43.560
I don't find any cool names.
我没找到什么酷炫的名字。

376
00:15:44.080 --> 00:15:44.360
Oh.
哦。

377
00:15:44.800 --> 00:15:45.840
So you can get up...
所以你可以……

378
00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:46.680
Here are your choices.
你的选择有这些。

379
00:15:46.940 --> 00:15:48.760
Pony keg, half keg, keg.
小啤酒桶、半桶、全桶。

380
00:15:49.960 --> 00:15:50.400
Hmm.
嗯。

381
00:15:51.140 --> 00:15:55.420
I feel like they sell more pony kegs just because the name is cute, but I don't know.
我觉得他们卖的小啤酒桶更多，纯粹是因为名字可爱吧，不过我也不确定。

382
00:15:55.420 --> 00:15:59.120
And you can carry them if you're on the petite side, like myself.
而且如果你像我一样娇小的话，还能抱得动它们。

383
00:15:59.760 --> 00:16:01.460
Oh, we're learning so much today.
哦，我们今天学到了好多。

384
00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:02.280
So much.
学到了太多。

385
00:16:02.840 --> 00:16:04.120
Fast fact number three.
冷知识之三。

386
00:16:04.460 --> 00:16:09.400
Angela, you were very, very, very pregnant in this episode.
安吉拉，这一集里你怀得很厉害很厉害很厉害。

387
00:16:09.740 --> 00:16:11.300
Yeah, I was.
对，确实很厉害。

388
00:16:11.640 --> 00:16:18.020
When you were filming your scenes with Dwight in the office, Lee Eisenberg had the flu.
当你在办公室里和德怀特拍对手戏时，李·艾森伯格得了流感。

389
00:16:18.200 --> 00:16:19.160
He was not there that day.
他那天不在现场。

390
00:16:19.340 --> 00:16:21.200
Only Gene Stepnitsky was on the set.
只有吉恩·斯特普尼斯基在片场。

391
00:16:21.200 --> 00:16:25.360
When they got into the editing bay to edit the episode, Lee Eisenberg was there.
等他们去剪辑室剪辑这一集时，李·艾森伯格来了。

392
00:16:25.520 --> 00:16:30.280
And he said, you guys, why don't we have any wider shots of these scenes?
然后他说，各位，为什么这些镜头都没有比较宽的远景呢？

393
00:16:30.540 --> 00:16:37.060
And Dave Rogers and Gene had to remind him because Angela's belly was very hard to hide.
戴夫·罗杰斯和吉恩只好提醒他，因为安吉拉的孕肚实在很难藏住。

394
00:16:37.520 --> 00:16:43.220
So all of these shots are like Angela from like the shoulders up.
所以所有这些镜头基本都是安吉拉肩膀以上的特写。

395
00:16:43.220 --> 00:16:46.280
But here is what else I found in my Googling, Angela.
不过安吉拉，我在谷歌上还查到了别的东西。

396
00:16:46.680 --> 00:16:47.220
What?
什么？

397
00:16:47.680 --> 00:16:51.660
By the time this episode aired, you had given birth.
这一集播出的时候，你已经生了。

398
00:16:52.100 --> 00:16:53.020
I know.
我知道。

399
00:16:53.400 --> 00:16:57.040
You gave birth five days before this episode aired.
你在这一集播出前五天生下了孩子。

400
00:16:57.380 --> 00:16:58.300
That is true.
确实如此。

401
00:16:58.720 --> 00:17:01.020
Well, lady, I have a really fun story from this episode.
好吧，女士们先生们，我这集有个非常有趣的故事。

402
00:17:01.280 --> 00:17:04.140
And it's something that involves the golf course.
而且这事儿跟高尔夫球场有关。

403
00:17:04.140 --> 00:17:06.420
I had no scenes at the golf course.
我在高尔夫球场没有戏份。

404
00:17:06.420 --> 00:17:08.760
But I went to visit the fellas.
但我去探望了那几个家伙。

405
00:17:08.760 --> 00:17:13.860
I was doing a whole series at this time on NBC.com called Adventures with Angela.
我当时在 NBC.com 主持一档系列节目，叫做《安吉拉历险记》。

406
00:17:14.420 --> 00:17:18.360
And Creed and Ed had written a song for my baby.
克里德和埃德为我的宝宝写了一首歌。

407
00:17:18.920 --> 00:17:22.140
I mean, with the banjo, the guitar, the whole thing.
我是说，有班卓琴、吉他，一应俱全。

408
00:17:22.380 --> 00:17:26.160
So I went to the golf course on Monday on their lunch.
所以我周一趁他们午休时去了高尔夫球场。

409
00:17:26.160 --> 00:17:30.080
And we sat out in this beautiful, green, like grassy area.
我们坐在那片美丽、翠绿的草地上。

410
00:17:30.620 --> 00:17:32.140
And they sang to me.
他们为我唱歌。

411
00:17:32.360 --> 00:17:36.700
And not only that, I couldn't remember how we got there.
不仅如此，我都记不清我们是怎么去的了。

412
00:17:36.820 --> 00:17:39.980
I was like, I don't remember driving to this place or where it was.
我就想，我不记得开车去过这地方，也不知道在哪儿。

413
00:17:40.100 --> 00:17:43.340
And you know when you're a passenger how you don't really pay attention as much?
你知道当你是乘客时，往往不会那么专注，对吧？

414
00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:43.960
Yeah.
是的。

415
00:17:44.700 --> 00:17:49.260
So I found this email that I had written to John Krasinski where I said,
所以我翻出了一封我写给约翰·卡拉辛斯基的邮件，里面写着：

416
00:17:49.620 --> 00:17:51.280
Hey, John, I'll see you Monday.
嘿，约翰，我们周一见。

417
00:17:51.280 --> 00:17:52.180
I can't wait.
我等不及了。

418
00:17:52.400 --> 00:17:54.500
Creed is picking me up in his sports car.
克里德要开他的跑车来接我。

419
00:17:54.660 --> 00:17:55.560
Should I be scared?
我该害怕吗？

420
00:17:55.560 --> 00:17:57.360
And we're going to come and have lunch.
我们要一起去吃午饭。

421
00:17:57.500 --> 00:18:00.800
And he and Ed are going to sing a song for my little baby.
他和埃德要为我的小宝宝唱首歌。

422
00:18:01.660 --> 00:18:04.720
Oh, so you rode in Creed's sports car?
哦，所以你是坐克里德的跑车去的？

423
00:18:04.980 --> 00:18:08.120
I rode in Creed's little two-seater sports car.
我坐的是克里德那辆小型双座跑车。

424
00:18:08.460 --> 00:18:10.420
And they sang this song to me.
他们为我唱了这首歌。

425
00:18:10.460 --> 00:18:12.160
And it was on NBC.com.
而且它当时在 NBC.com 上播出了。

426
00:18:12.280 --> 00:18:13.480
And Jenna, they gave me a copy.
珍娜，他们还给了我一份拷贝。

427
00:18:13.540 --> 00:18:17.660
And I tore my house up looking for this this week.
我这周把家里翻了个底朝天就为了找它。

428
00:18:17.780 --> 00:18:20.500
I have ransacked the whole house.
我把整栋房子都搜了个遍。

429
00:18:20.680 --> 00:18:22.460
I know I have it somewhere.
我知道我肯定把它放在某个地方。

430
00:18:22.460 --> 00:18:24.500
And I really wanted to play it for you guys.
我真的很想放给你们听。

431
00:18:24.500 --> 00:18:28.860
But Joya, who worked with us over at NBC.com, is on the case.
不过曾在 NBC.com 和我们合作过的乔亚正在帮忙找。

432
00:18:29.060 --> 00:18:29.960
She's going to find it.
她会找到的。

433
00:18:30.240 --> 00:18:34.540
And hopefully, maybe in a revisited, I'll be able to play it for you guys because it's
希望在之后的重温节目里，我能放给你们听，因为这真的很特别。

434
00:18:34.540 --> 00:18:35.280
really special.
真的特别特别。

435
00:18:35.280 --> 00:18:37.620
And I'm just heartbroken that I couldn't find it.
没能找到它，我简直心碎极了。

436
00:18:38.040 --> 00:18:40.260
That is so cool, Angela.
太酷了，安吉拉。

437
00:18:40.560 --> 00:18:42.520
I remember seeing the video of that.
我记得我看过那个视频。

438
00:18:42.520 --> 00:18:44.420
So I really do hope you find it.
所以我真的很希望你能找到它。

439
00:18:44.580 --> 00:18:45.380
Me too.
我也是。

440
00:18:45.380 --> 00:18:46.000
Me too.
我也是。

441
00:18:46.120 --> 00:18:46.760
It was so cute.
太可爱了。

442
00:18:46.900 --> 00:18:49.840
I remember Creed started off with, Angela's baby.
我记得克里德开头唱的是，“安吉拉的宝宝”。

443
00:18:50.440 --> 00:18:51.960
It was just so fun.
真的太有趣了。

444
00:18:52.500 --> 00:18:55.040
Well, and that's really all I had for this.
好吧，这就是我关于这集所有的存货了。

445
00:18:55.160 --> 00:18:59.560
I guess I have something that could be considered half a fast fact that I could throw in there.
我想我有一个勉强算得上半个快速事实的东西可以加进去。

446
00:18:59.840 --> 00:19:01.120
Half a fast fact?
半个快速事实？

447
00:19:01.260 --> 00:19:01.780
What you got?
你有什么料？

448
00:19:02.080 --> 00:19:07.340
My half a fast fact is that Toby was not in this episode because he was busy writing the
我的半个快速事实是，托比没有出演这一集，因为他忙着写季终集呢。

449
00:19:07.340 --> 00:19:08.080
season finale.
哦，这个料不错。

450
00:19:08.560 --> 00:19:10.660
Ooh, that is a good one.
哦，这个料不错。

451
00:19:10.860 --> 00:19:12.640
Well, I have a little Kinsey tidbit.
好吧，我有一个关于金茜的小八卦。

452
00:19:13.060 --> 00:19:15.880
Ooh, guess who found her script of job fair?
哦，猜猜谁找到了她当年《招聘会》那一集的剧本？

453
00:19:16.460 --> 00:19:17.260
This lady.
就是本小姐。

454
00:19:17.720 --> 00:19:18.680
Oh my gosh, Angela.
我的天哪，安吉拉。

455
00:19:18.820 --> 00:19:22.300
This is very exciting to me because I have a couple of fan questions that I didn't know
这让我非常兴奋，因为我有几个粉丝提出的问题，我之前并不知道

456
00:19:22.300 --> 00:19:24.420
the answer to, but I bet the answers are in the script.
答案，但我敢打赌答案就在剧本里。

457
00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:25.780
Ooh, ooh, let me get it.
哦，哦，让我去拿。

458
00:19:25.840 --> 00:19:26.260
I'll get it.
我去拿吧。

459
00:19:26.340 --> 00:19:30.080
And let's go to break and we'll come back and jump into some job fair.
我们先去休息一下，回来就开始聊聊《招聘会》。

460
00:19:30.640 --> 00:19:31.260
I like it.
我喜欢这样。

461
00:19:31.680 --> 00:19:42.340
All right.
好的。

462
00:19:42.340 --> 00:19:43.260
We are back.
我们回来啦。

463
00:19:43.440 --> 00:19:46.840
I have my script of job fair and Jenna right out of the gate.
我拿到了《招聘会》的剧本，詹娜，一开场

464
00:19:46.840 --> 00:19:48.300
I have a question for you.
我有个问题要问你。

465
00:19:48.460 --> 00:19:49.200
What is it?
什么问题？

466
00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:52.940
Did you notice that this episode does not have a cold open?
你有没有发现这一集没有片头前情提要？

467
00:19:53.240 --> 00:19:54.840
I kind of did, Angela.
我其实注意到了，安吉拉。

468
00:19:55.100 --> 00:19:58.900
We have a scene before the credits, but it's on plot.
我们在片名字幕前有一场戏，但它是推动剧情的。

469
00:19:58.900 --> 00:20:00.060
It's on story.
它是顺着故事发展的。

470
00:20:00.300 --> 00:20:04.180
It's not one of those standalone comedic cold opens that we're used to.
它不是那种我们习惯的独立搞笑片头。

471
00:20:04.320 --> 00:20:05.260
I did notice.
我确实注意到了。

472
00:20:05.480 --> 00:20:05.900
That's right.
没错。

473
00:20:06.000 --> 00:20:08.240
We just kind of get right into the meat of the episode, right?
我们基本上直接切入正题了，对吧？

474
00:20:08.540 --> 00:20:08.920
Yes.
是的。

475
00:20:09.100 --> 00:20:12.500
