00:33:49.320 --> 00:33:52.280
They had done this little Photoshop of David Denman.
奥斯卡有一个被删掉的采访镜头，他在里面说，

783
00:33:52.820 --> 00:33:53.340
Yeah.
不，说实话，我其实并没有从小就梦想着成为邓德米夫林的会计。

784
00:33:54.180 --> 00:33:55.480
In a high school photo.
在高中时，我也只是个普通孩子。

785
00:33:55.940 --> 00:33:58.720
And Oscar has a deleted talking head where he says,
成绩还不错，在新浪潮乐队里弹过贝斯，床头贴着一张金·贝辛格的海报。

786
00:33:59.200 --> 00:34:03.840
No, surprisingly enough, I did not always dream of being an accountant at Dunder Mifflin.
哦，我当时多么想成为金·贝辛格啊。

787
00:34:04.000 --> 00:34:06.200
In high school, I was just a normal kid.
那真是一个绝佳的采访镜头。

788
00:34:06.420 --> 00:34:12.720
I made decent grades, played bass in a new wave band, had a poster of Kim Basinger over my bed.
确实是。

789
00:34:13.000 --> 00:34:15.480
Oh, how I wanted to be Kim Basinger.
真希望它能保留在正片里。

790
00:34:15.480 --> 00:34:18.160
That is a great talking head.
迈克尔对自己的展位感到相当自信。

791
00:34:18.380 --> 00:34:19.320
It was.
自信到他随身带的唯一东西竟然是一张白纸。

792
00:34:19.520 --> 00:34:20.620
I wish it had stayed in.
所以就是他们四个人坐在桌子旁，面前摆着一张白纸。

793
00:34:21.320 --> 00:34:24.120
Michael is feeling pretty confident about his booth.
嗯，他说一张白纸等于无限可能。

794
00:34:24.480 --> 00:34:29.080
So much so that the only thing that he brought was a blank piece of paper.
这很概念化。

795
00:34:29.320 --> 00:34:33.700
So it's the four of them sitting at a table with a blank piece of paper in front of them.
他是这么说的。

796
00:34:33.860 --> 00:34:37.580
Well, he says a blank sheet of paper equals endless possibilities.
与此同时，隔壁的展位放着一个篮球框之类的东西。

797
00:34:37.960 --> 00:34:38.860
It's conceptual.
还有一个展位摆着爆米花机。

798
00:34:39.140 --> 00:34:40.100
That's what he says.
嗯。

799
00:34:40.420 --> 00:34:43.840
Meanwhile, the booth next door has like a basketball hoop.
嗯。

800
00:34:43.840 --> 00:34:45.700
And then one has like a popcorn machine.
嗯。

801
00:34:45.900 --> 00:34:48.120
No one is going to stop by this booth.
根本没有人会走到这个摊位前。

802
00:34:48.300 --> 00:34:51.880
And there's a deleted scene, Jenna, that goes on for so long.
珍娜，还有一个被删掉的场景，持续了超级久。

803
00:34:51.880 --> 00:34:59.420
I loved it so much of just a steady stream of kids walking past you guys, not stopping at all.
我太喜欢那个镜头了，源源不断的小孩从你们身边走过，完全不停留。

804
00:34:59.540 --> 00:35:06.120
And the only one that stops briefly sets down his popcorn-like container and just leaves it there like trash.
唯一一个停下来的人，随手放下他那个爆米花桶一样的容器，就像扔垃圾一样留在那儿。

805
00:35:06.200 --> 00:35:07.460
It spills over.
爆米花都撒出来了。

806
00:35:07.460 --> 00:35:10.460
And then Oscar is just tidying up this kid's trash.
然后奥斯卡就在那里默默收拾这个小孩留下的垃圾。

807
00:35:12.740 --> 00:35:15.900
Angela, we had so much fun shooting these scenes.
安吉拉，我们拍这些场景的时候可太开心了。

808
00:35:16.100 --> 00:35:19.820
I so loved getting to be on location with these three guys.
我特别喜欢能跟这三位伙计一起去外景地拍戏。

809
00:35:20.040 --> 00:35:21.900
We had the best time.
我们度过了最棒的时光。

810
00:35:22.120 --> 00:35:30.740
They gave all the background actors the direction that they should be like having a great time and smiling and high energy at all the other booths.
剧组给所有背景演员都下了指令，让他们在其他摊位前表现得玩得很开心、面带微笑且充满活力。

811
00:35:30.740 --> 00:35:34.440
So that when you got to ours, it was particularly quiet and sad looking.
这样一来，等走到我们这儿时，就显得格外冷清和凄凉。

812
00:35:34.980 --> 00:35:36.700
It really, really works.
这效果真的、真的很绝。

813
00:35:36.900 --> 00:35:38.320
It was cracking me up.
把我给笑死了。

814
00:35:38.620 --> 00:35:42.400
Should we go back over to Dunder Mifflin and see what everyone else is up to?
我们要不要回邓德米夫林看看其他人都在忙什么？

815
00:35:42.800 --> 00:35:43.240
Yes.
好呀。

816
00:35:43.420 --> 00:35:45.000
Well, let me tell you what they're up to.
那我来告诉你他们在忙什么。

817
00:35:45.140 --> 00:35:46.600
They're up to trying to sneak out of work.
他们在忙着偷溜早退。

818
00:35:46.780 --> 00:35:48.940
I mean, Meredith and Phyllis are stirring the pot.
我是说，梅雷迪思和菲利斯在挑拨离间。

819
00:35:49.180 --> 00:35:50.020
Michael is gone.
迈克尔不在。

820
00:35:50.220 --> 00:35:51.700
They don't want to stay the whole day.
他们不想待满整整一天。

821
00:35:52.040 --> 00:35:52.360
No.
没错。

822
00:35:52.620 --> 00:35:56.940
And Creed has a great line where he says he finished his work months ago.
克里德有一句超棒的台词，他说自己几个月前就把工作干完了。

823
00:35:57.160 --> 00:35:58.220
I loved that.
我太喜欢那句了。

824
00:35:58.620 --> 00:35:59.860
Like, what is he doing?
就感觉，他到底在干嘛？

825
00:36:00.740 --> 00:36:04.160
Dwight reminds them all that when Michael is gone, Jim is in charge.
德怀特提醒大家，迈克尔不在时，吉姆负责。

826
00:36:04.360 --> 00:36:06.400
And when Jim is gone, Andy and Dwight are in charge.
而吉姆不在时，安迪和德怀特负责。

827
00:36:06.560 --> 00:36:09.360
And when Andy is gone, you answer to Dwight.
而安迪不在时，你们就得听德怀特的。

828
00:36:09.660 --> 00:36:11.600
And Stanley's like, I don't give a crap.
然后斯坦利一副‘我才不在乎’的样子。

829
00:36:11.760 --> 00:36:12.100
I'm out.
‘我走人了。’

830
00:36:12.300 --> 00:36:15.640
I love so much that moment when Stanley walks out the door.
我太喜欢斯坦利摔门而出的那一刻了。

831
00:36:15.840 --> 00:36:16.600
I do, too.
我也是。

832
00:36:16.700 --> 00:36:18.300
And Dwight doesn't know what to do.
而且德怀特都不知道该怎么办。

833
00:36:18.540 --> 00:36:23.720
You know, we have said we feel like Stanley is the person Dwight is like, I am not going to mess with Stanley.
你知道的，我们一直觉得斯坦利就是那种会让德怀特觉得‘我可千万别去惹他’的人。

834
00:36:24.280 --> 00:36:30.500
But Dwight asserts to the whole office, look, you guys, the American work day ends at five o'clock.
但德怀特向全办公室重申：‘听着，各位，美国的工作日到五点才结束。’

835
00:36:30.740 --> 00:36:34.740
And so you must stay until the end of the work day, period.
‘所以你们必须待到工作日结束，没得商量。’

836
00:36:35.140 --> 00:36:36.600
Or I'll tattle on you.
‘不然我就去告发你们。’

837
00:36:37.080 --> 00:36:37.320
Right.
对吧。

838
00:36:38.680 --> 00:36:42.760
Back at the high school, Pam is chatting up a young prospective intern.
镜头回到高中，帕姆正在和一个年轻的潜在实习生聊天。

839
00:36:43.260 --> 00:36:46.280
He's actually interested in Dunder Mifflin.
他对邓德米夫林确实挺感兴趣。

840
00:36:46.280 --> 00:36:49.140
And Michael signals her to stop.
然后迈克尔示意她停下。

841
00:36:49.460 --> 00:36:49.760
Yeah.
对。

842
00:36:50.020 --> 00:36:51.140
Well, not just that.
嗯，不仅仅是这样。

843
00:36:51.340 --> 00:36:53.360
He goes up to this kid whose name is Justin.
他走到这个名叫贾斯汀的小孩面前。

844
00:36:53.720 --> 00:36:56.180
He says, I don't think this is the job for you.
他说：‘我觉得这工作不适合你。’

845
00:36:56.420 --> 00:36:58.360
Paper should be more of a hobby for you.
‘造纸对你来说应该更像是个业余爱好。’

846
00:36:58.720 --> 00:37:02.000
And then he takes away the kid's pamphlet that he was looking at.
接着他一把收走了这小孩刚才正在看的宣传册。

847
00:37:02.320 --> 00:37:02.620
Yeah.
没错。

848
00:37:02.620 --> 00:37:07.380
We had a fan catch about it, though, from Harmjen V and Alyssa C.
不过，我们收到了一条来自Harmjen V和Alyssa C的粉丝纠错。

849
00:37:07.640 --> 00:37:16.860
If Michael only brought one sheet of paper to the job fair, where did the brochure come from that Pam gave to Justin and Michael took away?
如果迈克尔去招聘会只带了一张纸，那帕姆给贾斯汀又被迈克尔拿走的宣传册是从哪儿来的？

850
00:37:17.620 --> 00:37:17.740
Hmm.
嗯……

851
00:37:18.620 --> 00:37:19.120
Good question.
好问题。

852
00:37:19.400 --> 00:37:21.300
I mean, clearly they brought a brochure.
我是说，很明显他们带了宣传册。

853
00:37:21.500 --> 00:37:27.360
I felt like the paper was their prop, was the thing that was supposed to be the eye-catching moment as people walked by.
我觉得那张纸就是他们的道具，是那种当人们走过时用来吸引眼球的东西。

854
00:37:27.360 --> 00:37:30.920
So maybe under the desk, Pam had some additional materials.
所以也许在桌子底下，帕姆准备了一些额外的材料。

855
00:37:31.380 --> 00:37:37.980
When the paper makes you stop in your tracks to talk to these people at their booth, then you get a pamphlet.
当那张纸让你停下脚步，去他们的展位和这些人交谈时，你就会拿到一份小册子。

856
00:37:38.260 --> 00:37:38.840
Okay.
好吧。

857
00:37:39.040 --> 00:37:39.700
I like it.
我喜欢。

858
00:37:40.500 --> 00:37:46.060
Michael is furious that Justin signed his name on their blank piece of paper.
迈克尔非常愤怒，因为贾斯汀在他们那张白纸上签了名。

859
00:37:46.280 --> 00:37:50.120
He's even more furious to learn that Pam only brought the one.
当得知帕姆只带了一张时，他更加愤怒了。

860
00:37:50.600 --> 00:37:50.940
Yeah.
是啊。

861
00:37:51.060 --> 00:37:52.960
And Pam's like, excuse me?
帕姆的反应就像是，不好意思？

862
00:37:53.140 --> 00:37:55.420
I love that she totally calls him out on it.
我喜欢她毫不留情地当面戳穿他。

863
00:37:55.580 --> 00:37:56.240
I know.
我知道。

864
00:37:56.240 --> 00:37:58.660
She said, Michael, do you not remember?
她说，迈克尔，你不记得了吗？

865
00:37:59.140 --> 00:38:03.500
I said, are you sure that we only need one sheet of paper?
我说，你确定我们只需要一张纸吗？

866
00:38:03.980 --> 00:38:07.240
And you said, yeah, we only need one sheet of paper to make a difference.
然后你说，对，我们只需要一张纸就能产生影响。

867
00:38:07.440 --> 00:38:11.220
And then you sneezed in my tea and said, don't worry, it's just allergies.
接着你在我的茶里打了个喷嚏，说，别担心，只是过敏。

868
00:38:12.000 --> 00:38:13.460
Pam, with the receipts.
帕姆掌握着证据。

869
00:38:13.840 --> 00:38:15.120
That's what the kids say, Jenna.
年轻人现在都这么说，珍娜。

870
00:38:15.460 --> 00:38:16.200
Oh, I like it.
哦，我喜欢。

871
00:38:16.760 --> 00:38:18.600
We had a fan question from Kate B.
我们收到了来自凯特·B的粉丝提问。

872
00:38:18.980 --> 00:38:22.760
When Justin signs his name on the piece of paper, he writes Justin E.
当贾斯汀在那张纸上签名时，他写的是贾斯汀·E。

873
00:38:22.760 --> 00:38:27.860
But later in the episode, he tells Michael that his last name is Paul Snick.
但在本集的后面，他告诉迈克尔他的姓是保罗·斯尼克。

874
00:38:28.400 --> 00:38:28.860
Explain.
解释一下。

875
00:38:29.400 --> 00:38:29.700
Hmm.
嗯。

876
00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:30.840
I'll tell you.
我来告诉你。

877
00:38:31.040 --> 00:38:32.120
I am intrigued.
我很感兴趣。

878
00:38:32.480 --> 00:38:38.020
The actor who plays Justin, his name is Trevor Einhorn.
扮演贾斯汀的演员，他的名字叫特雷弗·艾恩霍恩。

879
00:38:38.020 --> 00:38:41.180
Oh, so maybe he was writing his actual last name.
哦，所以也许他写的是他真正的姓。

880
00:38:41.540 --> 00:38:42.140
Yes.
是的。

881
00:38:42.340 --> 00:38:43.180
Isn't that amazing?
这不是很神奇吗？

882
00:38:43.620 --> 00:38:43.940
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

883
00:38:44.300 --> 00:38:49.000
So Trevor Einhorn has been a professional actor since he was five years old.
所以特雷弗·艾恩霍恩从五岁起就是一名专业演员了。

884
00:38:49.200 --> 00:38:53.880
And his breakout role was on the television comedy, Frasier.
他的成名作是喜剧电视剧《欢乐一家亲》。

885
00:38:53.880 --> 00:38:58.700
He played Frederick Crane, the son of Frasier and Lilith.
他饰演了弗雷德里克·克兰，也就是弗雷德里克和莉莉丝的儿子。

886
00:38:58.900 --> 00:39:00.200
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

887
00:39:00.560 --> 00:39:00.920
Yes.
是的。

888
00:39:01.300 --> 00:39:04.260
He also went on to have a recurring role on Mad Men.
他后来还在《广告狂人》中饰演一个常驻角色。

889
00:39:04.260 --> 00:39:07.320
He was in season six and seven as a copywriter.
他在第六季和第七季中饰演一名文案。

890
00:39:07.480 --> 00:39:12.280
And he also played Neil Kellerman in the ABC remake of Dirty Dancing.
他还曾在ABC翻拍的《辣身舞》中饰演尼尔·凯勒曼。

891
00:39:12.800 --> 00:39:13.260
Hmm.
嗯。

892
00:39:13.460 --> 00:39:17.600
He currently stars as Josh Hoberman in the sci-fi show The Magicians.
他目前在科幻剧《魔法师》中饰演乔什·霍伯曼。

893
00:39:17.740 --> 00:39:19.240
He is a Scorpio.
他是天蝎座。

894
00:39:19.420 --> 00:39:20.340
I'll have you know.
我得告诉你。

895
00:39:20.660 --> 00:39:21.860
That's new for a gueSt.
这对于嘉宾来说挺新鲜的。

896
00:39:21.860 --> 00:39:24.780
I don't feel like you've shared their Zodiac sign before.
我觉得你以前没分享过他们的星座。

897
00:39:25.040 --> 00:39:27.080
Is this a new part of the guest star breakdown?
这是嘉宾介绍的新环节吗？

898
00:39:27.540 --> 00:39:30.120
Well, it showed up in his bio, so I thought I'd throw it in there.
嗯，它出现在他的个人简介里，所以我想顺便提一下。

899
00:39:30.340 --> 00:39:30.540
Okay.
好吧。

900
00:39:30.940 --> 00:39:35.740
Finally, he is not related to our cinematographer, Randall Einhorn.
最后，他和我们的摄影指导兰德尔·艾恩霍恩没有任何亲戚关系。

901
00:39:36.200 --> 00:39:36.920
That is correct.
完全正确。

902
00:39:37.140 --> 00:39:38.360
Just a coincidence.
只是个巧合。

903
00:39:39.220 --> 00:39:42.580
Everyone back in the bullpen still really wants to sneak out.
大办公室里的每个人其实都还想偷偷溜走。

904
00:39:42.940 --> 00:39:44.380
They've waited for their moment.
他们一直在等一个机会。

905
00:39:44.560 --> 00:39:48.260
Dwight finally gets up and exits the bullpen to go to the bathroom.
德怀特终于起身离开大办公室去上洗手间。

906
00:39:48.580 --> 00:39:51.200
And Creed calls Angela to tell her they're all leaving.
然后柯里德打电话给安吉拉，告诉她大家都要走了。

907
00:39:51.200 --> 00:39:51.380
Hang.
等等。

908
00:39:51.440 --> 00:39:56.440
This scene made me laugh so hard, Jenna, because this is a bit that Creed and I still do.
珍娜，这个场景把我笑惨了，因为这是我和柯里德现在还会玩的梗。

909
00:39:56.780 --> 00:40:00.760
To this day, Creed will text me, Pumpkin's out.
直到今天，柯里德还会给我发短信说：“南瓜头出门了。”

910
00:40:01.280 --> 00:40:03.680
Or if we hang out, I'm like, all right, Creed, I'm going to go.
或者如果我们一起出去玩，我会说：“好了，柯里德，我要走了。”

911
00:40:03.820 --> 00:40:04.880
He'll say, Pumpkin's out.
他会说：“南瓜头出门了。”

912
00:40:05.020 --> 00:40:08.600
Like, he still says this to me after all of these years.
就像这样，时隔多年他还是会对我这么说。

913
00:40:08.980 --> 00:40:11.180
And this just warmed my heart.
这真的温暖了我的心。

914
00:40:11.400 --> 00:40:12.240
I loved it so much.
我太喜欢了。

915
00:40:12.360 --> 00:40:13.400
Sam, can you play the clip?
萨姆，你能播放一下这段视频吗？

916
00:40:29.100 --> 00:40:32.860
We got so much mail about this scene, Angela.
我们收到了很多关于这个场景的信件，安吉拉。

917
00:40:33.140 --> 00:40:37.960
People who listen to the podcast know that Creed calls you Pumpkin in real life.
听播客的人都知道柯里德现实生活中叫你“南瓜头”。

918
00:40:37.960 --> 00:40:44.360
And they wanted to know, was Creed ad-libbing in the scene and using his real life nickname for you?
他们想知道，柯里德在拍这场戏时是即兴发挥，用了他在现实中对你的昵称吗？

919
00:40:44.600 --> 00:40:46.580
Or was Pumpkin in the script?
还是剧本里本来就有“南瓜头”？

920
00:40:46.640 --> 00:40:49.100
And then he started calling you Pumpkin after this.
还是他从这之后才开始叫你“南瓜头”的？

921
00:40:49.420 --> 00:40:52.100
This scene is exactly as it is in the script.
这场戏跟剧本里写的一模一样。

922
00:40:52.340 --> 00:40:52.800
Exactly.
完全一样。

923
00:40:53.240 --> 00:40:55.200
So Creed did not improvise that.
所以柯里德并不是即兴发挥的。

924
00:40:55.340 --> 00:40:59.640
But I will tell you, ever since we shot Job Fair, he has called me Pumpkin.
但我得告诉你，自从我们拍完《招聘会》后，他就一直叫我“南瓜头”。

925
00:40:59.780 --> 00:41:01.660
To this day, he still calls me Pumpkin.
直到今天，他还是叫我“南瓜头”。

926
00:41:02.060 --> 00:41:03.060
That is so cute.
太可爱了。

927
00:41:03.060 --> 00:41:04.820
I know, it's so cute.
我知道，太可爱了。

928
00:41:05.100 --> 00:41:06.340
I loved that scene.
我好喜欢那个场景。

929
00:41:06.660 --> 00:41:10.620
Well, now Dwight comes out of the restroom and he sees that everyone has left.
好了，现在德怀特从洗手间出来，发现大家都走光了。

930
00:41:11.760 --> 00:41:13.360
Everyone except Angela.
除了安吉拉，所有人都走了。

931
00:41:14.060 --> 00:41:14.400
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

932
00:41:14.680 --> 00:41:18.020
Which makes total sense because she's the one other rule follower in this group.
这完全说得通，因为她这群人里另一个遵守规则的人。

933
00:41:18.560 --> 00:41:18.960
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

934
00:41:19.240 --> 00:41:23.080
There is a great scene that's deleted where Dwight comes out and he goes,
有一个很棒的被删减片段，讲的是德怀特出来后喊道：

935
00:41:23.260 --> 00:41:23.400
Ha!
哈！

936
00:41:23.780 --> 00:41:25.120
Last man standing.
笑到最后的人。

937
00:41:25.420 --> 00:41:27.980
And then Angela briskly walks past him and goes,
然后安吉拉从他身边快步走过，说道：

938
00:41:28.080 --> 00:41:28.760
Excuse me.
借过。

939
00:41:29.200 --> 00:41:32.660
And then there's a talking head that Angela has that really explains
接着安吉拉有一个单采镜头，真正解释了

940
00:41:32.660 --> 00:41:37.620
why she is just as eager to be one of the last people in the office.
为什么她也同样渴望成为办公室里留到最后的几个人之一。

941
00:41:39.300 --> 00:41:42.800
Whenever I'm here by myself, I like to pretend that all the others are dead.
每当办公室里只剩我一个人时，我喜欢假装其他人都死了。

942
00:41:44.320 --> 00:41:45.480
So this is nice.
所以这感觉挺好的。

943
00:41:47.660 --> 00:41:49.300
Oh my God, it made me laugh out loud.
天哪，这逗得我哈哈大笑。

944
00:41:49.400 --> 00:41:50.220
I spit out my water.
我把水都喷出来了。

945
00:41:50.360 --> 00:41:53.440
I went to take a sip of water while we were listening to the deleted scene.
我们在听那个被删减片段时，我正想喝口水。

946
00:41:53.580 --> 00:41:55.620
It seemed like a safe time to take a sip of water.
当时觉得那是喝口水的安全时间。

947
00:41:55.840 --> 00:41:57.960
But that, that was so good.
但是那个，真的太棒了。

948
00:41:58.180 --> 00:42:00.140
She pretends that everyone is dead.
她假装所有人都死了。

949
00:42:00.140 --> 00:42:02.620
And at the end, they had me do a little smile like that.
最后，他们让我微微一笑，就像这样。

950
00:42:02.700 --> 00:42:04.180
I was very delighted by this.
我对这个感到非常高兴。

951
00:42:04.960 --> 00:42:06.200
Oh, that is incredible.
哦，这太不可思议了。

952
00:42:07.120 --> 00:42:10.920
Well, Dwight's going to use this opportunity to call Michael and tattle.
德怀特会利用这个机会给迈克尔打电话告状。

953
00:42:11.100 --> 00:42:11.380
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

954
00:42:11.520 --> 00:42:12.700
He is very, very mad.
他非常非常生气。

955
00:42:13.500 --> 00:42:15.780
Michael is like, yeah, that makes total sense.
迈克尔的反应大概是，好吧，完全在理。

956
00:42:15.940 --> 00:42:16.480
Don't be weird.
别搞得怪里怪气的。

957
00:42:16.680 --> 00:42:17.560
Everyone should go home.
大家都该回家去。

958
00:42:17.740 --> 00:42:18.560
Why should they be there?
他们凭什么留在那儿？

959
00:42:18.780 --> 00:42:19.480
I'm not there.
我不在那儿。

960
00:42:19.580 --> 00:42:20.220
Jim's not there.
吉姆也不在那儿。

961
00:42:20.340 --> 00:42:20.860
Who cares?
谁在乎呢？

962
00:42:21.260 --> 00:42:21.440
Right?
对吧？

963
00:42:22.400 --> 00:42:24.960
Oh, Dwight is so sad.
噢，德怀特太惨了。

964
00:42:24.960 --> 00:42:28.040
I know, but Dwight isn't going to go home.
我知道，但德怀特是不会回家的。

965
00:42:28.160 --> 00:42:29.560
He has personal standards.
他有他自己的原则。

966
00:42:29.560 --> 00:42:33.440
He's going to work his day and he's going to dock everyone else's pay.
他会把今天的工作干完，然后扣掉所有其他人的工资。

967
00:42:33.680 --> 00:42:34.680
He's going to try.
他会试图这么做的。

968
00:42:35.080 --> 00:42:41.280
Back at the job fair, Pam has gone into her old art room to get a sheet of paper.
镜头回到招聘会现场，帕姆走进了她以前的美术教室去拿一张纸。

969
00:42:41.580 --> 00:42:43.960
I titled this scene Brutal.
我给这个场景起名叫“残酷”。

970
00:42:45.900 --> 00:42:50.030
Once one moment of her glory days, right?
曾经属于她的辉煌时刻，对吧？

971
00:42:50.290 --> 00:42:50.950
One moment.
就那么一个时刻。

972
00:42:50.950 --> 00:42:54.030
She's going to show the camera her piece of art.
她要向镜头展示她的那件艺术品。

973
00:42:54.270 --> 00:42:55.790
Surely it's still on the wall.
说不定它还挂在墙上呢。

974
00:42:56.470 --> 00:42:58.270
Yeah, we got a lot of mail about this.
对，我们收到了很多关于这部分的信件。

975
00:42:58.430 --> 00:43:02.270
People wanted to know what exactly is Pam looking for on the wall?
大家很想知道帕姆到底在墙上找什么？

976
00:43:02.530 --> 00:43:03.530
Was it artwork?
是一件艺术品吗？

977
00:43:03.730 --> 00:43:04.630
Was it an award?
是一个奖项吗？

978
00:43:05.170 --> 00:43:11.170
They wanted to know if there was more to this scene and also just what was my take on this?
他们想知道这场戏背后是不是还有更多内容，以及我对此作何感想？

979
00:43:11.730 --> 00:43:18.990
I'll tell you, the idea was that when Pam was in school, a piece of her art was put on the wall
我来告诉你，当时的构思是，帕姆上学时，她的作品曾被挂在墙上

980
00:43:18.990 --> 00:43:22.470
on display and it was a big moment for her that she was very proud of.
公开展出，这对她来说是个非常自豪的重要时刻。

981
00:43:22.670 --> 00:43:29.890
And she very, very quickly, as soon as she says, maybe it's still there, realizes that like a decade
而她非常非常快地，就在她说出“也许它还在那儿”的时候，意识到距离这个让她如此自豪的时刻

982
00:43:29.890 --> 00:43:34.810
has gone by since this moment that she was so proud of.
已经过去了大约十年。

983
00:43:34.950 --> 00:43:39.870
Probably the last moment that her art was held up for admiration.
这大概也是她的艺术作品最后一次受到人们的赞赏。

984
00:43:40.390 --> 00:43:43.230
Because remember, her art show didn't go great.
因为记住，她的画展办得并不顺利。

985
00:43:43.230 --> 00:43:43.470
Right.
没错。

986
00:43:44.250 --> 00:43:52.490
And so she just has this crushing, like you said, brutal realization that a lot of time has gone by
所以她才有了这种正如你所说、极其沉重且残酷的觉悟：距离她投入精力发展这部分的自己

987
00:43:52.490 --> 00:43:58.070
since she invested in this part of herself and she's quickly embarrassed and has to just stuff it down
已经过去了很长时间，她瞬间感到很尴尬，只能强压下这种情绪

988
00:43:58.070 --> 00:43:58.590
and walk away.
然后走开。

989
00:43:59.030 --> 00:44:03.270
Well, it is exactly the same in the script as what you see in the episode.
剧本里的描写跟你在剧集里看到的一模一样。

990
00:44:03.570 --> 00:44:04.050
Yeah.
对。

991
00:44:04.530 --> 00:44:05.870
In the script, it says,
剧本里写道：

992
00:44:06.010 --> 00:44:11.410
Pam comes up to a room that is labeled art room and goes inside and walks confidently to the supply desk.
帕姆走到一个标有美术教室的房间前，走了进去，自信地走向供应台。

993
00:44:11.410 --> 00:44:14.330
She finds a blank piece of paper and shows it to the camera.
她找到一张白纸，把它展示给镜头。

994
00:44:14.850 --> 00:44:15.490
Pam says,
帕姆说：

995
00:44:15.730 --> 00:44:16.410
My old art room.
我的旧美术教室。

996
00:44:16.550 --> 00:44:18.210
Hey, I wonder if it's still here.
嘿，不知道它还在不在。

997
00:44:18.390 --> 00:44:21.610
She looks around at the walls that have some student artworks on them.
她环顾四周，墙上贴着一些学生的艺术作品。

998
00:44:22.250 --> 00:44:22.670
Nope.
没有。

999
00:44:22.930 --> 00:44:24.070
They must have taken it down.
他们肯定已经把它撤下来了。

1000
00:44:24.370 --> 00:44:25.070
Never mind.
算了。

1001
00:44:25.550 --> 00:44:26.030
Yeah.
是啊。

1002
00:44:26.430 --> 00:44:27.130
It's hard.
这很难。

1003
00:44:27.290 --> 00:44:30.130
It's hard to realize that you've put your hopes and dreams on hold.
意识到自己把希望和梦想都搁置了，这感觉很难受。

1004
00:44:30.530 --> 00:44:30.930
Yeah.
是啊。

1005
00:44:31.230 --> 00:44:32.610
And she does in this moment.
她在这个时刻确实意识到了。

1006
00:44:33.090 --> 00:44:37.850
You know, after all that, Pam brings this piece of paper to Michael and it's wrong.
你知道的，经历了这一切之后，帕姆拿了这张纸给迈克尔，结果拿错了。

1007
00:44:38.070 --> 00:44:40.090
He wanted Dunder Mifflin card stock.
他想要邓德米夫林的卡片纸。

1008
00:44:40.090 --> 00:44:43.150
He doesn't want this stupid, random piece of paper.
他才不想要这种愚蠢的、随随便便的纸。

1009
00:44:43.330 --> 00:44:44.630
He sends her back to the office.
他把她打发回办公室。

1010
00:44:45.190 --> 00:44:45.370
Yeah.
是啊。

1011
00:44:45.470 --> 00:44:50.570
He said, I don't want this Pendleton crap, which I looked up online and I couldn't find
他说，我才不要这什么彭德尔顿的破纸，我在网上查了，根本没找到

1012
00:44:50.570 --> 00:44:51.310
Pendleton paper.
彭德尔顿纸。

1013
00:44:51.470 --> 00:44:53.230
I did find Pendleton business cards.
我倒是找到了彭德尔顿的名片。

1014
00:44:53.510 --> 00:44:57.350
But he says, Pam, I want the ultra white card stock.
但他说，帕姆，我要的是超白卡片纸。

1015
00:44:57.930 --> 00:45:00.830
Pam drives all the way back to Dunder Mifflin.
帕姆一路开车回了邓德米夫林。

1016
00:45:01.350 --> 00:45:01.530
Yeah.
是啊。

1017
00:45:01.750 --> 00:45:06.190
And she goes and gets the ultra white card stock out of the copier.
然后她去复印机里把超白卡片纸拿了出来。

1018
00:45:06.190 --> 00:45:11.610
Dwight looks puzzled and rightly so, because I don't think that paper lives in the copier.
德怀特看起来很困惑，这也是理所当然的，因为我觉得那种纸平时不放在复印机里。

1019
00:45:11.950 --> 00:45:12.810
Just going to say.
我只想说这个。

1020
00:45:13.010 --> 00:45:16.230
Well, let me tell you something about copiers, Angela.
好吧，安吉拉，让我跟你说说复印机的事。

1021
00:45:16.590 --> 00:45:23.210
She pulls it from a specialty drawer in the copier, not from the main paper feed of the
她是从复印机的一个专用抽屉里抽出来的，而不是从那个

1022
00:45:23.210 --> 00:45:25.350
copier, which could have held copy paper.
能装普通复印纸的主进纸盒里拿的。

1023
00:45:25.690 --> 00:45:30.770
Perhaps in our special drawer, you can select for when you want card stock.
也许在我们这个特殊的抽屉里，你可以选择什么时候需要卡片纸。

1024
00:45:30.770 --> 00:45:34.790
Look, well, I saw that she pulled it from the low drawer, Jenna.
听着，詹娜，我看到她是低头从那个抽屉里拿的。

1025
00:45:35.010 --> 00:45:39.410
I saw that and not the other drawer, but I just think it would be on the shelf.
我看到了，不是从别的抽屉，但我只是觉得它应该放在架子上。

1026
00:45:40.150 --> 00:45:40.530
So.
所以。

1027
00:45:41.450 --> 00:45:46.030
Well, if it had been on the shelf, it wouldn't have been as good of a shot between Dwight
好吧，如果它放在架子上，德怀特和安吉拉之间就不会有那么棒的镜头效果了

1028
00:45:46.030 --> 00:45:46.530
and Angela.
。

1029
00:45:46.670 --> 00:45:48.150
So it had to come out of the copier.
所以它必须从复印机里出来。

1030
00:45:48.350 --> 00:45:48.650
All right.
好吧。

1031
00:45:48.950 --> 00:45:50.150
That's the real reason.
这才是真正的原因。

1032
00:45:50.410 --> 00:45:51.330
OK, fine.
好吧，行。

1033
00:45:51.450 --> 00:45:51.730
Fine.
行吧。

1034
00:45:52.430 --> 00:45:57.010
Well, we're about to go back to the golf course and there's a lot to talk about.
我们要回高尔夫球场了，还有很多事情要聊。

1035
00:45:57.370 --> 00:46:00.570
I think maybe we should take a break and then we'll get into it.
我想我们也许该休息一下，然后再继续深入。

1036
00:46:00.770 --> 00:46:08.090
After we've refreshed ourselves and emptied our bladders, I will wash my hands.
等我们神清气爽、排空膀胱之后，我会去洗手。

1037
00:46:08.250 --> 00:46:11.830
If you need to know who Jenna's going to be at 70, you just heard her.
如果你想知道詹娜七十岁时是什么样，刚才听她说话就知道了。

1038
00:46:12.010 --> 00:46:14.850
After we have refreshed ourselves and emptied our bladders.
等我们神清气爽、排空膀胱之后。

1039
00:46:15.370 --> 00:46:17.050
All right, guys, we'll be right back.
好了，各位，我们马上回来。

1040
00:46:27.320 --> 00:46:27.860
All right.
好的。

1041
00:46:27.960 --> 00:46:28.740
We are back.
我们回来了。

1042
00:46:29.140 --> 00:46:31.000
Mr. McGuire is struggling with his ball.
麦奎尔先生正在跟他的球较劲。

1043
00:46:31.220 --> 00:46:32.180
I like that.
我喜欢这样。

1044
00:46:33.860 --> 00:46:36.780
He's struggling with his ball in the sand trap.
他在沙坑里跟他的球较劲呢。

1045
00:46:36.780 --> 00:46:38.660
He can't get it out of the sand, Jenna.
詹娜，他怎么都把球打不出沙坑。

1046
00:46:39.290 --> 00:46:41.020
And he doesn't want anyone to help him.
而且他不想让任何人帮他。

1047
00:46:41.140 --> 00:46:41.880
He wants to do it himself.
他想自己来。

1048
00:46:42.160 --> 00:46:44.940
And listen, Andy is just such a hot mess.
听着，安迪真是个彻头彻尾的烂摊子。

1049
00:46:45.120 --> 00:46:47.220
He's having all of his rage issues.
他的暴躁脾气全发作了。

1050
00:46:47.480 --> 00:46:50.640
He's got on his pants that have little pheasants on them.
他穿着印有小野鸡图案的裤子。

1051
00:46:50.940 --> 00:46:55.580
It's not going to make him happy when Jim gets a phone call from Pam while Andy's trying
当安迪正准备挥杆时，

1052
00:46:55.580 --> 00:46:56.140
to swing.
吉姆却接到了潘的电话，这绝对不会让他高兴。

1053
00:46:56.560 --> 00:46:57.840
No, it is not.
不，确实不会。

1054
00:46:57.840 --> 00:47:01.640
And Jim is really trying to recruit Mr. McGuire.
而且吉姆真的在极力拉拢麦圭尔先生。

1055
00:47:01.800 --> 00:47:03.440
And McGuire is a big no.
但麦圭尔态度坚决地拒绝了。

1056
00:47:03.740 --> 00:47:05.420
He's just like, no, no, no.
他就是一副拒绝、拒绝、再拒绝的样子。

1057
00:47:05.720 --> 00:47:07.080
He just wants to play golf.
他只想打高尔夫球。

1058
00:47:07.300 --> 00:47:11.860
Well, so does Andy, because he proposes that they race to the next hole.
安迪也是这么想的，因为他提议比赛看谁先到下一个洞。

1059
00:47:12.080 --> 00:47:14.580
He hops in the golf cart and crashes it.
他跳上高尔夫球车然后撞了车。

1060
00:47:14.760 --> 00:47:15.880
He goes flying.
他整个人飞了出去。

1061
00:47:16.120 --> 00:47:18.480
The roof of the golf cart is ripped off.
高尔夫球车的顶棚被整个掀掉了。

1062
00:47:18.640 --> 00:47:21.100
This is a major golf cart crash.
这可是一场严重的高尔夫球车撞击事故。

1063
00:47:21.280 --> 00:47:23.920
I mean, I feel like this was a big stunt for us.
我是说，我觉得这对我们来说算是一个大特技动作了。

1064
00:47:24.200 --> 00:47:24.920
It was.
确实是。

1065
00:47:24.920 --> 00:47:26.120
We got a lot of mail about it.
我们为此收到了大量的邮件。

1066
00:47:26.200 --> 00:47:28.900
People wanted to know, did Ed do this stunt?
人们想知道，这个特技是埃德自己做的吗？

1067
00:47:29.360 --> 00:47:30.780
No, no, no, no, no.
不，不，不，不，不。

1068
00:47:30.800 --> 00:47:30.940
Of course not.
当然不是。

1069
00:47:31.100 --> 00:47:31.760
No, no, no, no.
不，不，不，不。

1070
00:47:31.940 --> 00:47:33.060
It was a stunt driver.
那是特技替身演员。

1071
00:47:33.500 --> 00:47:37.920
We also got questions about everyone's actual golfing ability.
我们还收到了关于每个人实际高尔夫水平的提问。

1072
00:47:38.460 --> 00:47:42.860
Thomas V wants to know, did any of these guys actually play golf?
托马斯·V想知道，这里面有人真的会打高尔夫吗？

1073
00:47:43.940 --> 00:47:48.720
Well, well, well, well, we will tell you.
嗯，嗯，嗯，嗯，我们会告诉你们的。

1074
00:47:48.960 --> 00:47:49.360
We know.
我们知道。

1075
00:47:49.800 --> 00:47:54.680
I reached out to Ed and he said that before this episode, he had never been a
我联系了埃德，他说在拍这集之前，他从来没打过

1076
00:47:54.680 --> 00:47:59.800
golfer and that the show gave everybody lessons so that they could look like they knew what
